       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. That is about 5 times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg** three times daily\n- **1,000 mg** twice daily (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is what you intend, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking it with pharmacy first."
